WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:54.575
Diary management puts the shared plan into practice Diary management is more than finding an empty calendar slot. The executive may need preparation time, a decision-ready pack, travel time and contributions from other people. A new appointment must be checked against those commitments and the purpose they serve. In the fictional Meridian case, Lindiwe needs time to prepare for a service-investment decision meeting . Daniel, her executive assistant ( EA ), coordinates the plan. Finance and operations supply papers, Thandi, the executive protection officer (EPO) , provides protective input within her mandate , and Aisha may provide cover only for work she has accepted. You will use this connected plan throughout LU1. First you will distinguish known facts from assumptions, then prepare the executive support brief ( T1.1 ), examine authority and diary conflicts, recommend workable options and develop a working agreement . Each new task uses information or a work product from the preceding learning.
